  "stem": "The expression \\((7x - 2)(x + 6) - 3x(x + 4)\\) is equivalent to \\(ax^{2} + bx + c\\), where \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\) are constants. What is the value of \\(b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "28"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Expand the product: \\((7x - 2)(x + 6) = 7x^{2} + 42x - 2x - 12 = 7x^{2} + 40x - 12\\).",
    "Expand the second term: \\(3x(x + 4) = 3x^{2} + 12x\\).",
    "Subtract: \\(7x^{2} + 40x - 12 - 3x^{2} - 12x = 4x^{2} + 28x - 12\\), so \\(b = 28\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\np = Poly(expand((7*x - 2)*(x + 6) - 3*x*(x + 4)), x)\nassert p.coeff_monomial(x) == 28\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [28]",
